@* Both of upstream's: a spinner as an inline-end addon on a single-line control, and a spinner
   in a block-end addon under a textarea, sharing that row with a label and the send button.

   Both controls are disabled, which is the point — the spinner is there because the field is
   busy, and a field that is busy is a field you cannot type into. *@
<div class="flex w-full max-w-md flex-col gap-4">
    <InputGroup>
        <InputGroupControl placeholder="Send a message..." disabled />
        <InputGroupAddon Align="inline-end"><Spinner /></InputGroupAddon>
    </InputGroup>

    <InputGroup>
        <InputGroupControl Multiline rows="2" placeholder="Send a message..." disabled />
        <InputGroupAddon Align="block-end">
            <Spinner /> Validating...
            <InputGroupButton Variant="default" Size="icon-sm" Class="ms-auto">
                <Icon Name="arrow-up" /><span class="sr-only">Send</span>
            </InputGroupButton>
        </InputGroupAddon>
    </InputGroup>
</div>
